Z||000000||fierobaby||06-24-2001||01:30 AM||||Hey all I finally went to my first Fiero show today! it was a great show with some very nice Fieros I am sure that someone will post the winners! I met a Few of you people from off here including Kslish Roger and Eric and otheres! it was great meeting all of you and I hope we will meet again. maybe next time you can all see my Fiero!<P>well I love you all!<p>[This message has been edited by fierobaby (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||rogergarrison||06-24-2001||08:21 PM||||nice to meet you and your bf too. it was a fun afternoon hanging out with all you guys.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Au nrod||06-24-2001||09:01 PM||||we are delighted you all had a good time at the c.o.f.e. car show in wooster. fierobaby, i'm truly sorry i did meet you personally. i keep waiting for that candyapple red car to show up, but my time was in vain. i did meet several others of the forum folks. it truly was great. mark your calendars for june next year, because we will do it again since we had a pretty good turnout for the first year. thanks to all that came by, and to you who miss the show  -  you missed the FIERO FUN.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierobaby:<BR><B>Hey all I finally went to my first Fiero show today! it was a greta show with soem very nice Fieros I am sure that someone will post the winners! I met a Few of you people from off here including Kslish Roger and Eric and otheres! it was great meeting all of you and I hope we will meet again. maybe next time you can all see my Fiero!<P>well I love you all!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eric||06-25-2001||09:57 AM||||I had a really good time meeting all of you also.  Sorry I had to leave so early, I guess I knew I really didn't stand a chance competing against sub 10,000 mile 88 GTs.<P>I know I'm not really a member of COFE so I'm probably way out of line suggesting this but I think it would be more interesting for everybody if the club did a cruise or something around the back roads of Wooster.  A bunch of people told me about some good twisty roads they took on the way up, and I think it would add a certain "active" element to the whole event.  It should serve to attract a bigger group for next year's event too.  I probably speak for a lot of people, who didn't bother to come to the show, when I say I'm not too keen on being judged.  I'm sure it's a great thrill for somebody with a perfect car, but I drive my car a bunch.  Keeping my car perfect is not an option.  I think if COFE could attract that croud too, they would have a great event.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierokid87||06-25-2001||11:26 AM||||ERIC you left and when they had the awards you got third!  or was it second.  I dont know.  you did get something though.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||3
Z||000005||Au nrod||06-25-2001||11:28 AM||||eric,<P>your right on both counts, the cruise or tour and the judging. we did have an 18 mile tour of the campus set up, but most everyone said they did not want to do that. second, originally we had the classes broken up into mileage groups; something like  up to 30,000; 30,001 to 60,000; 60,001 to 90,000 and etc., but with the smaller number of cars we omitted that this year. hopefully in the future we will classify the cars that way. i too feel overwhelmed up against some of the low mileage beauties. i can't compete against something like that. we did and do think independent judges is the only way to go. we think they did an outstanding job. we'll do better next year. and oh, by the way, you too can be a member of c.o.f.e.. check out <A HREF="http://www.ohiofiero.com" TARGET=_blank>www.ohiofiero.com</A>  for an application.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Eric:<BR><B>I had a really good time meeting all of you also.  Sorry I had to leave so early, I guess I knew I really didn't stand a chance competing against sub 10,000 mile 88 GTs.<P>I know I'm not really a member of COFE so I'm probably way out of line suggesting this but I think it would be more interesting for everybody if the club did a cruise or something around the back roads of Wooster.  A bunch of people told me about some good twisty roads they took on the way up, and I think it would add a certain "active" element to the whole event.  It should serve to attract a bigger group for next year's event too.  I probably speak for a lot of people, who didn't bother to come to the show, when I say I'm not too keen on being judged.  I'm sure it's a great thrill for somebody with a perfect car, but I drive my car a bunch.  Keeping my car perfect is not an option.  I think if COFE could attract that croud too, they would have a great event.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><p>[This message has been edited by Au nrod (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||1
